1
00:00:00,203 --> 00:00:02,757
Studying abroad starts with a practical question:

2
00:00:03,085 --> 00:00:04,539
what will the whole journey cost?

3
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:09,093
StudyFlow connects that answer to a loan plan and controlled payments.

4
00:00:09,737 --> 00:00:11,156
Ask in your own words.

5
00:00:11,396 --> 00:00:15,297
Tuition, living costs and essential expenses appear together as

6
00:00:15,297 --> 00:00:16,589
a full-course estimate.

7
00:00:16,825 --> 00:00:19,811
The breakdown keeps sourced fees and estimates visible, so

8
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:21,612
you can see what the total depends on.

9
00:00:21,848 --> 00:00:24,540
Housing and everyday living costs are included,

10
00:00:24,857 --> 00:00:28,684
along with essentials such as insurance, visa costs and travel.

11
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:31,790
With four universities side by side, you can compare

12
00:00:31,790 --> 00:00:34,633
the whole course, its length and its annual cost.

13
00:00:34,869 --> 00:00:37,400
Switch the same comparison into Chinese yuan,

14
00:00:37,426 --> 00:00:40,339
or U.S. dollars, using reference exchange rates.

15
00:00:40,575 --> 00:00:43,642
When a ranking is unavailable, the assistant says so

16
00:00:43,642 --> 00:00:45,524
and points to a source for checking.

17
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:48,086
It can also explain the campus and nearby food

18
00:00:48,086 --> 00:00:50,142
before bringing you back to the next decision.

19
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:53,617
Once you choose a school, the conversation carries that

20
00:00:53,617 --> 00:00:56,518
context forward and asks how much you want to borrow.

21
00:00:56,775 --> 00:01:00,470
Here, forty-eight thousand baht produces a recommended plan with

22
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:04,848
the monthly payment, interest, fees and total repayment.

23
00:01:05,098 --> 00:01:07,621
Other calculated plans remain available when you want to

24
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:08,740
compare the options.

25
00:01:08,976 --> 00:01:11,337
The loan panel also keeps the inputs and full

26
00:01:11,337 --> 00:01:13,694
repayment schedule available for a closer look.

27
00:01:13,929 --> 00:01:16,298
If the monthly payment feels too high, say so.

28
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:19,844
StudyFlow recalculates and shows how both the payment and

29
00:01:19,844 --> 00:01:21,124
total interest change.

30
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:25,036
The study-loan example also shows interest-only payments during study,

31
00:01:25,318 --> 00:01:27,965
followed by principal and interest repayments.

32
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,724
Prefer less interest overall?

33
00:01:29,959 --> 00:01:32,702
The assistant compares shorter terms and makes the higher

34
00:01:32,702 --> 00:01:34,133
monthly commitment visible.

35
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:35,875
You can reduce the amount too.

36
00:01:36,135 --> 00:01:38,517
This plan now borrows thirty thousand baht;

37
00:01:38,801 --> 00:01:42,423
the school cost never silently becomes the requested loan.

38
00:01:42,672 --> 00:01:46,133
If you are not interested, recommendations pause, even while

39
00:01:46,133 --> 00:01:47,841
you ask another school question.

40
00:01:48,077 --> 00:01:50,619
An explicit request resumes the discussion.

41
00:01:50,855 --> 00:01:54,161
Earlier recommendations cannot submit an outdated plan.

42
00:01:54,803 --> 00:01:57,060
Asking to apply opens a review of the current

43
00:01:57,060 --> 00:02:00,845
terms. Only the student's confirmation submits the application.

44
00:02:01,081 --> 00:02:04,144
A simulated admission notice is attached automatically.

45
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:07,454
It is not a real university offer or a bank approval.

46
00:02:07,690 --> 00:02:10,537
The bills already show the loan's proposed share, while

47
00:02:10,537 --> 00:02:11,957
payment waits for signing.

48
00:02:12,192 --> 00:02:15,417
The student marks the remaining demo document declarations ready,

49
00:02:15,722 --> 00:02:19,433
then reviews and explicitly signs the agreement as a separate action.

50
00:02:19,669 --> 00:02:22,655
The signed loan schedules payments to the school's verified

51
00:02:22,655 --> 00:02:26,760
simulation account, without putting the loan proceeds in the student's wallet.

52
00:02:27,370 --> 00:02:29,403
Preparation stays in the conversation:

53
00:02:29,662 --> 00:02:32,250
a dated request becomes a saved reminder.

54
00:02:32,490 --> 00:02:34,500
Mark a task completed when it is done,

55
00:02:34,759 --> 00:02:37,440
or undo that update if it still needs attention.

56
00:02:37,676 --> 00:02:40,372
A partly covered tuition bill shows the loan's share

57
00:02:40,372 --> 00:02:42,764
and the amount the student still needs to pay, together.

58
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,442
When the wallet is short, the demo offers a

59
00:02:45,442 --> 00:02:48,007
clearly marked simulated top-up for the remainder.

60
00:02:48,243 --> 00:02:50,785
The student then confirms the payment with a password.

61
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:54,169
The bill and balance update together, and the loan-covered

62
00:02:54,169 --> 00:02:56,109
amount cannot be charged again.

63
00:02:56,737 --> 00:03:00,621
Separate currency balances keep the source of each simulated payment clear.

64
00:03:00,862 --> 00:03:04,114
For an exchange, the assistant compares quotes and prepares

65
00:03:04,114 --> 00:03:06,112
a proposal for the student to review.

66
00:03:06,348 --> 00:03:10,325
A wrong password stops the action and leaves the balance unchanged.

67
00:03:10,487 --> 00:03:14,777
After password confirmation, five hundred yuan is debited, and

68
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:18,027
the quoted amount in Thai baht is credited after fees.

69
00:03:18,262 --> 00:03:22,957
For a transfer, routes, fees and expected arrival come before commitment.

70
00:03:23,206 --> 00:03:27,820
Confirmation debits one thousand yuan and creates a traceable transfer order.

71
00:03:28,075 --> 00:03:30,517
We advance the clearly labelled demo date to the

72
00:03:30,517 --> 00:03:32,203
delivery window's final day.

73
00:03:32,438 --> 00:03:35,598
The simulated channel marks the transfer delivered, and its

74
00:03:35,598 --> 00:03:37,631
status is visible in the history.

75
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:41,082
When a loan installment falls due, it appears with

76
00:03:41,082 --> 00:03:42,363
its amount and date.

77
00:03:42,603 --> 00:03:45,423
Before committing, the student reviews the installment,

78
00:03:45,589 --> 00:03:47,981
then authorizes the repayment with a password.

79
00:03:48,217 --> 00:03:51,585
The installment becomes paid, the wallet is debited, and

80
00:03:51,585 --> 00:03:53,456
the movement remains in the ledger.

81
00:03:54,103 --> 00:03:57,390
For a new recipient, an operator first reviews and

82
00:03:57,390 --> 00:03:58,613
verifies the payee.

83
00:03:58,853 --> 00:04:02,182
Even a correct password cannot bypass a transfer limit.

84
00:04:02,418 --> 00:04:05,446
The request enters the operations workbench for review.

85
00:04:05,682 --> 00:04:09,046
The person who verified the payee cannot approve the transfer.

86
00:04:09,282 --> 00:04:12,970
A separate operator checks the amount, recipient and purpose,

87
00:04:13,251 --> 00:04:15,458
then explicitly confirms the decision.

88
00:04:15,694 --> 00:04:18,363
The approval is recorded, but moves no money.

89
00:04:18,599 --> 00:04:21,558
The student must still authorize submission with a password.

90
00:04:21,793 --> 00:04:25,099
Clear costs, informed decisions and controlled payments:

91
00:04:25,393 --> 00:04:27,715
all demonstrated with simulated funds.
